        {
          "title": "Asymptotic Notation and Growth Rates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Bounds",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Big-O==: `f(n)=O(g(n))` if `f ≤ c·g(n)` for all `n ≥ n0`",
                "An ==upper bound==, usually quoted for the **worst case**",
                "==Omega== is the lower bound: `f ≥ c·g(n)`",
                "==Theta== is the tight bound: true only when {green:O} and {blue:Omega} both hold"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Symbol",
                "Bound",
                "Means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "O",
                  "upper",
                  "at most g"
                ],
                [
                  "Omega",
                  "lower",
                  "at least g"
                ],
                [
                  "Theta",
                  "tight",
                  "O and Omega"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Simplify and Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Drop **constants** and lower-order terms: `3n²+5n+9` is ==Theta(n²)==",
                "Different input variables stay separate: `O(a+b)`, not `O(n)`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Growth order, slowest to fastest",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "log n",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n log n",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n²",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n³",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2ⁿ",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n!",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Big-O Is Not Worst Case",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Big-O bounds a **function**; it is just notation",
                "==Best==, ==average== and ==worst== case are separate functions",
                "Each has its own O, Omega and Theta"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Big-O is a bound on a function, not a synonym for worst case. Theta needs both O and Omega."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Analysing Loops and Amortised Cost",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Analysing Loops and Amortised Cost",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Counting Loops",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Shape",
                "Cost"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Loop to n",
                  "==O(n)=="
                ],
                [
                  "Nested, both to n",
                  "**multiply**: O(n²)"
                ],
                [
                  "Sequential loops",
                  "**add**, larger wins"
                ],
                [
                  "i doubles or halves",
                  "==O(log n)=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "i = 1",
                "while i < n:",
                "    i *= 2  # log2(n) steps"
              ],
              "note": "binary search halves the range: O(log n)"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Amortised Cost",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Amortised== = average cost per operation over a **worst-case sequence**",
                "No probability involved",
                "Dynamic array doubles capacity: n appends cost O(n) total, so {green:O(1) amortised}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Append",
                    "sub": "O(1)",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Full: resize",
                    "sub": "copy n, O(n)",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Capacity x2",
                    "sub": "cheap again",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Amortised",
                "Average case"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Holds for",
                  "**every** sequence",
                  "assumed input distribution"
                ],
                [
                  "Randomness",
                  "none",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "One resize is O(n), yet appends are O(1) amortised. Hash table resize is amortised too."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Is amortised the average case?** No: it is guaranteed for any sequence",
                "**Cost of binary search?** O(log n), the range halves each step"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
