    {
      "title": "The Call Stack and Recursion Anatomy",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Call Stack and Recursion Anatomy",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stack Frames",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each call ==pushes a frame==: **parameters**, **locals**, **return address**",
                "Returning ==pops== the frame",
                "Frames unwind ==last-in first-out==",
                "Depth d costs ==O(d)== stack space, even with no extra data structure"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "push 3",
                    "sub": "fact(3) waits",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "push 2",
                    "sub": "fact(2) waits",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "push 1",
                    "sub": "base: returns 1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pop",
                    "sub": "2 * 1 = 2",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "pop",
                    "sub": "3 * 2 = 6",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Anatomy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Base case}: returns directly, no recursive call",
                "{blue:Recursive case}: moves ==strictly toward== the base case"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def fact(n):",
                "    if n <= 1:           # base case",
                "        return 1",
                "    return n * fact(n - 1)  # toward base"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing or unreachable base case gives ==infinite recursion==",
                "`n - 2` with base case `n == 0`: odd n goes 5, 3, 1, -1 and skips 0"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Check every recursion",
              "text": "Does each call get **strictly closer** to a base case that it can actually ==hit==?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Recursion Trees and Recurrences",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
